## 5. Phase Plan

```
Phase 0 (hours): Worktree stabilization
  - Clean M report.html, ?? .claude/, ?? scripts/analysis/ in bathos
  - Commit or stash before any dispatch
  - No code changes; pure git hygiene

Phase 1 (1 day, independent):
  - Item #9: PostToolUse NLM hook (praxia only)
  - No bathos changes; safe to run in parallel with Phase 0

Phase 2 (3-4 days, bathos only):
  - Items #1 + #2 + #3: exception-swallowing + manifest + outcome="error"
  - Single coherent diff: runner.py / sidecar.py / prereg.py / compact.py / schema.py
  - Schema bump v4 → v5 (adds manifest_sha256, manifest_path, outcome_error_reason, adversarial_check_status)
  - Dependency: Phase 0 must be clean

Phase 3 (~1 week, parallelizable):
  - Bathos track: Items #4 + #6 (structured MCP errors + adversarial_check)
  - Praxia track: Item #10 (Rust gate error taxonomy)
  - Dependency: Phase 2 must be complete (item #4 extends item #1's GateError work)

Phase 4 (~1 week, parallelizable with Phase 3 tail):
  - Items #5 + #7 + #8 (sprint-audit signals + bth cite + bth lineage prov)
  - Dependency: Item #3 (error_rate metric depends on outcome="error")
  - Items #7 + #8 depend on Phase 2 schema (manifest_sha256 in citation)

Phase 5 (~1 week, deps Phase 3):
  - Items #11 + #12 (sprint-composer gate + loop budget)
  - Entry gate: locate sprint-composer first; may surface scope change
  - Dependency: Item #10 (Rust gate error types)
```

**Dependency arrows:**
```
Phase 0 → Phase 2 → Phase 3 (bathos) → Phase 4
                  ↘ Phase 3 (praxia) → Phase 5
Phase 1 (independent)
```

